<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Logic & Theory | Bolt Compass</title>

    <link href="https://unpkg.com/aos@2.3.1/dist/aos.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/tippy.js@6/animations/scale.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>

    <div id="header-placeholder"></div>

    <main>
        <section class="container" style="padding-top: 4rem;">
            <div data-aos="fade-up">
                <h1 style="color: var(--accent-blue);">Theoretical Foundation & Logic</h1>
                <p>The Bolt Compass architecture is predicated on a synthesized model of multiple intelligences, designed to quantitatively measure subjective human aptitudes.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="chart-container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="200">
                <h2>The 6 Intelligence Categories</h2>
                <p>To provide a robust profile, the system categorizes user inputs into six primary vectors. Click below to expand the operational definition of each vector.</p>

                <div class="accordion">
                    <button class="accordion-header">Linguistic Intelligence</button>
                    <div class="accordion-content">
                        <div class="accordion-content-inner">
                            <p>Evaluates the capacity to manipulate syntax, semantics, and pragmatics. Assessed through text-heavy scenario parsing and communication preference modeling.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accordion">
                    <button class="accordion-header">Logical-Mathematical</button>
                    <div class="accordion-content">
                        <div class="accordion-content-inner">
                            <p>Measures deductive reasoning, pattern recognition, and <span class="tooltip-trigger" data-tippy-content="The ability to evaluate complex datasets to draw algorithmic conclusions.">algorithmic thinking</span>. Key indicator for STEM-aligned career pathways.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accordion">
                    <button class="accordion-header">Visual-Spatial</button>
                    <div class="accordion-content">
                        <div class="accordion-content-inner">
                            <p>Assesses the capacity to mentally manipulate 2D and 3D space, heavily weighted in design, architecture, and structural engineering matching.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accordion">
                    <button class="accordion-header">Interpersonal</button>
                    <div class="accordion-content">
                        <div class="accordion-content-inner">
                            <p>Evaluates social cognition, empathy, and the ability to interpret non-verbal communicative cues. Critical for management and consultative roles.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accordion">
                    <button class="accordion-header">Intrapersonal</button>
                    <div class="accordion-content">
                        <div class="accordion-content-inner">
                            <p>Measures self-regulation, metacognition, and autonomous task-management capabilities under varying stress conditions.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accordion">
                    <button class="accordion-header">Naturalistic</button>
                    <div class="accordion-content">
                        <div class="accordion-content-inner">
                            <p>Observes pattern recognition in organic or chaotic systems. Initially derived from ecological sciences, applied here to complex systems analysis and macroscopic trends.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="300" style="margin-top: 4rem;">
                <h2>The 6-Layer Assessment Schema</h2>
                <p>The assessment relies on a progressively complex input schema. We refer to this as the <strong>6-Layer Pipeline</strong>. By segregating question types into discrete layers, the algorithm effectively mitigates <span class="tooltip-trigger" data-tippy-content="A cognitive bias where a user attempts to select answers they believe are 'correct' rather than accurate to their nature.">social desirability bias</span>.</p>
                <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 2rem;">
                    <div style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                        <h4 style="color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Layers 1-3: Foundational</h4>
                        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom:0;">These layers capture baseline physiological and immediate cognitive responses to standard stimuli using a 1-5 Likert scale.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                        <h4 style="color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Layers 4-6: Synthesized</h4>
                        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom:0;">Advanced multi-variate selection and situational judgment tests. These layers demand higher cognitive load to accurately reflect real-world problem-solving tendencies.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <div id="footer-placeholder"></div>

    <!-- Scripts -->
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/@popperjs/core@2"></script>
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/tippy.js@6"></script>
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/aos@2.3.1/dist/aos.js"></script>
    <script src="components.js"></script>
    <script src="scripts.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
