<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Scoring Methodology | Bolt Compass</title>

    <link href="https://unpkg.com/aos@2.3.1/dist/aos.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/tippy.js@6/animations/scale.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">

    <!-- Chart.js -->
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
</head>
<body>

    <div id="header-placeholder"></div>

    <main>
        <section class="container" style="padding-top: 4rem;">
            <div data-aos="fade-up">
                <h1 style="color: var(--accent-blue);">Scoring Methodology & Accuracy</h1>
                <p>The reliability of the Bolt Compass stems from its strict mathematical approach to scoring. Raw inputs are processed, normalized, and aggregated to form a statistical composite.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="chart-container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="200">
                <h2>The Scoring Algorithm</h2>
                <p>Responses from the user interface (ranging from 1 to 5) are mapped to their corresponding intelligence categories via the schema defined in the assessment layers.</p>

                <div class="formula-block">
                    Score_C = ( &Sigma; v_i ) / n
                </div>

                <p>Where: <br>
                <strong>Score_C</strong> is the final score for Category C. <br>
                <strong>v_i</strong> is the value of response i mapped to Category C. <br>
                <strong>n</strong> is the total number of questions evaluating Category C.</p>

                <p>This results in an average score (between 1.0 and 5.0) for every intelligence category.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="chart-container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="300">
                <h2>Interactive Data Visualization</h2>
                <p>Use the radar chart below to visualize how raw data maps onto the 6 intelligence vectors. <span style="color: var(--accent-blue); font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer;" id="randomizeData">Click here to generate a random data distribution.</span></p>

                <div style="max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 0;">
                    <canvas id="scoringChart"></canvas>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="400" style="margin-top: 4rem;">
                <h2>Profile Consistency Metric</h2>
                <p>Beyond raw scores, the algorithm calculates a <strong>Profile Consistency</strong> metric. This measures the variance across all six categories, indicating whether a user has highly specialized skills (high variance, lower consistency score) or generalized aptitude (low variance, high consistency score).</p>
                <div class="formula-block">
                    Consistency = 100 - [ ( Max_Score - Min_Score ) / 5 * 100 ]
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <div id="footer-placeholder"></div>

    <script src="https://unpkg.com/@popperjs/core@2"></script>
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/tippy.js@6"></script>
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/aos@2.3.1/dist/aos.js"></script>
    <script src="components.js"></script>
    <script src="scripts.js"></script>
    <script>
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
            const ctx = document.getElementById('scoringChart').getContext('2d');
            let dataValues = [4.2, 3.8, 2.5, 4.8, 3.2, 3.9];

            const scoringChart = new Chart(ctx, {
                type: 'radar',
                data: {
                    labels: ['Linguistic', 'Logical-Math', 'Visual-Spatial', 'Interpersonal', 'Intrapersonal', 'Naturalistic'],
                    datasets: [{
                        label: 'Intelligence Vector Score (1-5)',
                        data: dataValues,
                        backgroundColor: 'rgba(29, 78, 216, 0.2)',
                        borderColor: 'rgba(29, 78, 216, 1)',
                        pointBackgroundColor: 'rgba(29, 78, 216, 1)',
                        pointBorderColor: '#fff',
                        pointHoverBackgroundColor: '#fff',
                        pointHoverBorderColor: 'rgba(29, 78, 216, 1)',
                        borderWidth: 2
                    }]
                },
                options: {
                    responsive: true,
                    scales: {
                        r: {
                            angleLines: { color: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)' },
                            grid: { color: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)' },
                            pointLabels: {
                                font: { size: 14, family: "'Inter', sans-serif" },
                                color: '#1e293b'
                            },
                            min: 0,
                            max: 5,
                            ticks: { stepSize: 1, backdropColor: 'transparent' }
                        }
                    },
                    plugins: {
                        legend: { display: false }
                    }
                }
            });

            document.getElementById('randomizeData').addEventListener('click', () => {
                const newData = Array.from({length: 6}, () => (Math.random() * 4 + 1).toFixed(1));
                scoringChart.data.datasets[0].data = newData;
                scoringChart.update();
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
